From 70b997f384a17c91cf2709aff2a8c69b01c4c966 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chu Qinghao <6337103+qinghao1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Headless player: run the game without rendering
 (ENABLE_HEADLESS)

A build with ENABLE_HEADLESS runs the whole player (table script, physics,
plugins like PinMAME, animations, audio) without drawing anything, for hosts
that render the table themselves or need no picture at all, like automated
tests. The host drives it one frame at a time through
Player::StepHeadlessFrame() and reads the state it needs from the parts.

- BGFX runs the Noop backend, initialized on the game thread: no swap chain,
  no render thread, frames submitted by the renderer execute inline
- The player skips the 3D scene and texture loading, and runs without display
- Windows count as focused, like VR ones, so play is never paused for focus
- Closing the playfield window skips the canvas style reset when the module
  has no canvas, as a headless one does
- Accessing a uniform missing from a shader does nothing (reads return a
  neutral value), as the Noop backend reports none. Other builds still
  assert, except for the stereo only 'layer' uniform as before

Builds without ENABLE_HEADLESS behave the same.
